<title>USA: Network Long Distance sees Q1 charge.</title>
<headline>Network Long Distance sees Q1 charge.</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT NEWS, Va. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Network Long Distance Inc said Thursday it expects a one-time charge of about $2.3 million in the first quarter ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>The company said the charge will reflect transaction costs related to its mergers with National Teleservices Inc and Eastern Telecom International Corp.</p>
<p>Network Long Distance also said that its loss of $7.8 million in the fiscal year ended March 31 included a non-recurring non-cash provision of $6.3 million, reflecting the reduced carrying value of previously purchased customer bases and goodwill.</p>
</text>
